# Testing-feature capabilities (EXCP Time)

This repo uses **Testing-feature** (`tc`). Vendor features are synced into **`.testing-feature/docs/`** by **`tc project sync`** / **`tc project update`**.

## Keep sync current

After **Testing-feature** vendor changes or when `tc project check-updates` reports drift:

```bash
tc project update
```

Rebuild the linked CLI once per machine after vendor pulls:

```bash
cd /path/to/Testing-feature && npm run link:dev
```

## Capability index

Read **`.testing-feature/docs/capabilities.md`** for the full list. Highlights:

| Feature | Entry |
|---------|--------|
| Session queue + status | `tc ui` → **Session** |
| Fix-proof recording | `.testing-feature/docs/session-recording.md` — max **5 clips/Key**, `test-runs/current/evidence/` |
| Blockers + agent fix | **Blockers** tab / `tc blockers` |
| Impact | `tc impact --git` / auto-impact on linked app edits |
| Backend xUnit | `.cursor/rules/backend-automated-tests.mdc` — backend Keys → xUnit + `dotnet test` |

## Agent tasks

- **Product behavior** changes → update `test-cases/**` specs and **Related code** in the same task.
- **Tool-only** behavior (new `tc` / `tc ui` feature) → run **`tc project update`** here; vendor self-tests stay in the Testing-feature repo unless the product needs new QA rows.

Do not commit `.testing-feature/`, `test-runs/`, or other local-only paths.
